{
  "title": "Particle-in-cell / PIC",
  "html": "<h1>Particle-in-cell / PIC</h1><p>Plasma PIC represents a distribution by computational particles and self-consistent fields by a mesh. Its smoothing, collisionality and sampling error differ from direct all-pairs Coulomb dynamics.</p><h2 id=\"model\">Problem and representative equations</h2><p>Start with nonrelativistic electrostatic Vlasov–Poisson. Computational particle p has weight wₚ, charge qₚ and position xₚ. Dimensionless shape weights Sᵢ sum to one, and Vᵢ is cell volume. Deposit ρ, solve Poisson with the stated boundary conditions, and use E=−∇φ.</p><div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>p</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"/><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">v</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">E</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_i=\\frac1{V_i}\\sum_p w_pq_pS_i(\\mathbf x_p),\\qquad -\\nabla_h^2\\phi_i=\\rho_i/\\epsilon_0,\\qquad \\dot{\\mathbf v}_p=(q_p/m_p)\\mathbf E_h(\\mathbf x_p).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ρ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.7076em;vertical-align:-1.3861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span c